## The durable cure (landed s1651, takes effect on the NEXT runner restart)

`scripts/lane-runner-v3.sh` now resolves a codex client that meets the floor **before**
consuming a master, and REFUSES the dispatch — leaving the master in its queue — when no
such client exists. That converts this outage from "masters silently shredded at 14s
each" into "runner refuses loudly and loses nothing". It is inert for the currently
running instance, which parsed the script at 05:08; a restart is still required.
